I added `__builtin_expect` hints so the compiler lays out the rare invalid cases out-of-line and keeps the single load on the fall-through fast path, avoiding branch-layout penalties in the hot decode loop; behaviour is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile == NULL, 0) ||
        __builtin_expect(profileIndex >= profile->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```